{"id": "EUVD-2026-82986", "enisaUuid": "e5427a19-9c18-3e79-afde-dddb0c331acc", "description": "uri-js through 4.4.1 contains a denial of service vulnerability in the removeDotSegments function that loops infinitely when a path segment begins with Unicode line or paragraph separators. Attackers can trigger this by calling removeDotSegments directly or through normalize/resolve functions with IRI handling enabled, causing the Node.js event loop to block indefinitely until heap exhaustion.", "datePublished": "2026-09-18T15:06:04", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-24T14:23:06", "baseScore": 8.7, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/garycourt/uri-js/issues/105", "https://github.com/garycourt/uri-js", "https://github.com/garycourt/uri-js/blob/4.4.0/src/uri.ts#L349", "https://github.com/garycourt/uri-js/blob/4.4.0/src/uri.ts#L352-L376", "https://www.npmjs.com/package/uri-js/v/4.4.1", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/uri-js-through-4.4.1-denial-of-service-via-removedotsegments"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-93690", "GHSA-ffpj-9hx9-929p"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.45, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "9b0ddf45-ca96-3332-8116-0b26a2493d38", "product": {"name": "uri-js", "vendor": {"name": "garycourt"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22644.4.1"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "9f085b81-32c6-3ed7-b8e5-91785eef8112", "vendor": {"name": "garycourt"}}], "isExploited": false}